<title>JAPAN: Chip-related shares up on Intel's solid earnings.</title>
<headline>Chip-related shares up on Intel's solid earnings.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of semiconductor-related firms jumped in Tuesday morning trade, encouraged by news of solid earnings for U.S. chipmaker Intel Corp, traders said. On Monday, Intel reported third quarter earnings of $1.48 per share, which was higher than analysts' expectations.</p>
<p>As of 0156 GMT, the share price of Advantest Corp surged 120 yen to 4,510 yen on volume of 116,300 shares. Oki Electric Industry was up 15 yen at 740 yen, on volume of 1.65 million shares.</p>
<p>NEC Corp, a major semiconductor maker, was also up 20 yen at 1,280 yen. The volume was 1.554 million shares.</p>
